{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21fd7e39d99b57bc5bd4", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Probability - Test 5", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 75, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0d7"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d07f", "title": "Mathematics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d018", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "The coefficients <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> of the quadratic equation, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;are obtained by throwing a dice three times. The probability that this equation has equal roots is:"}, "options": [{"id": "6e0be6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>72</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d019"}, {"id": "9675d2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d01a"}, {"id": "3371ad", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>54</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d01b"}, {"id": "a3f79f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>216</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d01c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d01d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b450c"], "question": {"text": "If $A$ and $B$ are two events such that $P(A \\cap B)=0.1$, and $P(A \\mid B)$ and $P(B \\mid A)$ are the roots of the equation $12 x^2-7 x+1=0$, then the value of $\\frac{\\mathrm{P}(\\overline{\\mathrm{A}} \\cup \\overline{\\mathrm{B}})}{\\mathrm{P}(\\overline{\\mathrm{A}} \\cap \\overline{\\mathrm{B}})}$ is :"}, "options": [{"id": "02736c", "text": "$\\frac{4}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d01e"}, {"id": "316637", "text": "$\\frac{7}{4}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d01f"}, {"id": "2823d9", "text": "$\\frac{5}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d020"}, {"id": "3d77d2", "text": "$\\frac{9}{4}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d021"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d022", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117afaec5f0702080bde0f1"], "question": {"text": "A six faced die is biased such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>P</mi></math>(a prime number)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>P</mi></math>(a composite number)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> be a random variable that counts the number of times one gets a perfect square on some throws of this die. If the die is thrown twice, then the mean of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "7a64b6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d023"}, {"id": "2235e9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d024"}, {"id": "fc0e44", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d025"}, {"id": "df7848", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d026"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d027", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["6117b03dc5f0702080bdea7d"], "question": {"text": "Let $\\mathrm{S}=\\{1,2, \\ldots . ., 20\\}$. A subset $\\mathrm{B}$ of $\\mathrm{S}$ is said to be \"nice\", if the sum of the elements of $\\mathrm{B}$ is 203 . Than the probability that a randomly chosen subset of $S$ is \"nice\" is :"}, "options": [{"id": "093451", "text": "$\\frac{7}{2^{20}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d028"}, {"id": "915a59", "text": "$\\frac{5}{2^{20}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d029"}, {"id": "c46774", "text": "$\\frac{4}{2^{20}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d02a"}, {"id": "1fde80", "text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d02b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d02c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b450c"], "question": {"text": "Bag<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mi>A</mi></math> contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> white, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> red balls and bag <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> white, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> red balls. One bag is selected at random and a ball is drawn from it. The probability of drawing the ball from the bag <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, if the ball drawn in white, is :"}, "options": [{"id": "4ce468", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d02d"}, {"id": "18a798", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d02e"}, {"id": "ef529e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d02f"}, {"id": "cf3319", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d030"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d031", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117afaec5f0702080bde0f1"], "question": {"text": "<p>A coin is biased so that the head is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> times as likely to occur as tail. This coin is tossed until a head or three tails occur. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;denotes the number of tosses of the coin, then the mean of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e8563c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>38</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d032"}, {"id": "820593", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d033"}, {"id": "fae440", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d034"}, {"id": "4b3d29", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>81</mn><mn>64</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d035"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d036", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "Out of 11 consecutive natural number if three numbers are selected at random (without repetition), then the probability that they are in A.P. with positive common difference is :"}, "options": [{"id": "ad6b00", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>101</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d037"}, {"id": "655ab3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>101</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d038"}, {"id": "8bef47", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>33</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d039"}, {"id": "a558b9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>99</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d03a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d03b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b450c"], "question": {"text": "Box <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;contains&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math>&nbsp;cards numbered <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math>&nbsp;and Box <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> contains&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math>&nbsp;cards numbered&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>31</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math>. A box is selected at random and a card is drawn from it. The number on the card is found to be a non-prime number. The probability that the card was drawn from Box&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> is&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "0cf079", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d03c"}, {"id": "54496e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>17</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d03d"}, {"id": "9774de", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>17</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d03e"}, {"id": "400fda", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d03f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d040", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117afaec5f0702080bde0f1"], "question": {"text": "A bag contains 30 white balls and 10 red balls. 16 balls are drawn one by one randomly from the bag with replacement. If $X$ be the number of white balls drawn, then\n\n$\\left(\\frac{\\text { mean of } \\mathrm{X}}{\\text { standard deviation of } \\mathrm{X}}\\right)$ is equal to:"}, "options": [{"id": "9c99f5", "text": "4", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d041"}, {"id": "f6ebfe", "text": "$4 \\sqrt{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d042"}, {"id": "f752e0", "text": "$3 \\sqrt{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d043"}, {"id": "2c9d80", "text": "$\\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d044"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d045", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["6117b03dc5f0702080bdea7d"], "question": {"text": "The probability that a relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is both symmetric and transitive, is equal to:"}, "options": [{"id": "e9216e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathM