_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0b9"}, {"id": "1fda7f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0ba"}, {"id": "652f80", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0bb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0bc", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "Let $\\mathrm{a}, \\mathrm{b}$ and $\\mathrm{c}$ denote the outcome of three independent rolls of a fair tetrahedral die, whose four faces are marked $1,2,3,4$. If the probability that $a x^2+b x+c=0$ has all real roots is $\\frac{m}{n}$, $\\operatorname{gcd}(\\mathrm{m}, \\mathrm{n})=1$, then $\\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{n}$ is equal to ________"}, "options": [{"id": "aab34a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0bd"}, {"id": "7a3f9f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0be"}, {"id": "f3a943", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0bf"}, {"id": "404e37", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0c0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0c1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b4519"], "question": {"text": "In an examination, there are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> true-false type questions. Out of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>, a student can guess the answer of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> questions correctly with probability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and the remaining <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;questions correctly with probability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. If the probability that the student guesses the answers of exactly&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> questions correctly out of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>27</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>10</mn></msup></mfrac></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "4b3be2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0c2"}, {"id": "c27a1f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0c3"}, {"id": "746ea9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0c4"}, {"id": "4c41d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0c5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0c6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117b07bc5f0702080bdef7b"], "question": {"text": "Four fair dice are thrown independently 27 times. Then the expected number of times, at least two dice show up a three or a five, is"}, "options": [{"id": "4134e0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0c7"}, {"id": "6a116a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0c8"}, {"id": "a16b48", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0c9"}, {"id": "47b362", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0ca"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1e2ee0e063d923d0cb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "If the probability that a randomly chosen <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>-digit number formed by using digits&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1<